<http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#DramaticIrony> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "One dimension revealing information another dimension does not provide in memes, e.g. text revealing information visuals don't show"@en .
<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01258#mapping_1> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The text 'ladies! if your man is offended by this' directly refers to the visual of the woman smoking. The visual entity 'smoking_woman_scene' is the concrete instantiation of 'this' in the text. The mapping is explicit through the juxtaposition of the text and the visual, where the woman's action (smoking) is the object of the man's supposed offense, as stated in the text."@en .
<http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#Semi-transparentOverlay> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Text that blends with underlying visual content through transparency in memes"@en .
