<http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#BackgroundPreservation> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Text placed only over neutral areas to preserve important visual content in memes"@en .
<http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#geometricallyAdjacentTo> <http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#relationIndex> "18"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> .
<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01258#smoking_woman_scene> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A woman with dark skin tone and curly hair, wearing sunglasses and denim overalls, is holding and smoking a cigarette. The scene is framed to focus on her as the central subject, with a blurred background suggesting an outdoor public setting. The text overlay is positioned above and below her, framing her as the subject of the meme's message."@en .
<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01258#overallintent_instance> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "meme-id: ladies_if_your_man_is_offended_by_this_he_is_a_faggot_end_of_story; hasOverallIntent: hateful; overall-intent-description: The image depicts a woman with dark skin tone and curly hair, wearing sunglasses and overalls, smoking a cigarette. The text overlay reads: 'ladies! if your man is offended by this he is a faggot. end of story.' The overall intent is to deliver a hateful message by using a visual of a woman smoking (a behavior often stereotyped as 'edgy' or 'rebellious') to justify a derogatory label ('faggot') against men who disapprove of it. This is a direct attack on men based on their sexual orientation or gender expression, using a stereotypical visual to reinforce a harmful stereotype. The meme is designed to provoke and insult, fitting the category of hateful content as it targets individuals based on protected characteristics (sexual orientation) and uses degrading language."@en .
<http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#faceMasking> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
